      {
        "id": "lem-qft-example-spin-trace-completeness",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "library": "mathematics",
        "title": "Clifford traces and normalized spin completeness",
        "statement": "Use the finite Dirac matrices and adjoint of [[def-qft-dirac-projections]], and the separate geometric metric $\\eta=\\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$ and algebraic contraction $h=-\\eta=\\operatorname{diag}(1,-1,-1,-1)$ of [[def-qft-example-data]]. Write $p=(E,\\mathbf p)$ for an energy four-vector with components in joules, $M\\geq0$ for a rest-energy parameter in joules, and $E=\\sqrt{|\\mathbf p|^2+M^2}>0$. In the natural-length variables of the Dirac definition, $\\mathbf k=\\mathbf p/(\\hbar c)$, $\\mu=M/(\\hbar c)$, and $\\omega=E/(\\hbar c)$.\n\nLet $\\beta=\\gamma^0$, $\\alpha_j=\\beta\\gamma^j$, $\\Sigma_j=\\operatorname{diag}(\\sigma_j,\\sigma_j)$, and $\\gamma_5=i\\gamma^0\\gamma^1\\gamma^2\\gamma^3$. Define $H_\\pm=\\boldsymbol\\alpha\\cdot\\mathbf p\\pm\\beta M$ and $P_\\pm=(I_4+H_\\pm/E)/2$. Each $P_\\pm$ is a Hermitian rank-two projection. Choose orthonormal bases $\\xi_{\\pm,1},\\xi_{\\pm,2}$ of their ranges and put $u_s=\\sqrt{2E}\\xi_{+,s}$ and $v_s=\\sqrt{2E}\\xi_{-,s}$ for $s=1,2$. With $\\bar z=z^\\dagger\\beta$ and $\\not p=\\gamma^0E-\\sum_j\\gamma^jp_j$, the following hold:\n\n$$\\operatorname{Tr}I_4=4,\\quad \\operatorname{Tr}\\gamma^a=0,\\quad \\operatorname{Tr}(\\gamma^a\\gamma^b)=4h^{ab},\\quad \\operatorname{Tr}(\\gamma^a\\gamma^b\\gamma^c)=0,$$\n\n$$\\operatorname{Tr}(\\gamma^a\\gamma^b\\gamma^c\\gamma^d) =4(h^{ab}h^{cd}-h^{ac}h^{bd}+h^{ad}h^{bc}), \\qquad \\sum_s u_s\\bar u_s=\\not p+M,\\quad \\sum_s v_s\\bar v_s=\\not p-M.$$\n\nThe columns satisfy $(\\not p-M)u_s=0$ and $(\\not p+M)v_s=0$. For all $x,y\\in\\mathbb C^4$, complex conjugation of a Dirac current is $\\overline{\\bar x\\gamma^a y}=\\bar y\\gamma^a x$. The Countable Choice hypothesis written in the current draft [[def-qft-dirac-projections]] is retained as a supplier assumption; this finite-dimensional proof makes no additional choice use.",
        "deps": [
          "def-qft-example-data",
          "def-qft-dirac-projections"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-qft-example-data": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-qft-dirac-projections": "mathematical-premise"
        },
        "dependency_level": 2,
        "proof_strategy": "direct",
        "provenance": {
