      {
        "id": "cor-qft-example-scalar-tree-coefficients",
        "kind": "corollary",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "library": "mathematics",
        "title": "Scalar symmetry factors and decay coefficient units",
        "statement": "Let $m\\geq0$ be a scalar rest energy in joules, and let $p_1,p_2,k_1,k_2$ be the incoming and outgoing scattering vectors on the positive $m$-shell of [[def-qft-example-two-body-phase-space-data]], so each $(E,\\mathbf q)$ satisfies $E=\\sqrt{|\\mathbf q|^2+m^2}>0$. Require $p_1+p_2=k_1+k_2=P$ and $s=h(P,P)>4m^2$, with $h$ as in [[def-qft-example-data]]. Evaluate the coefficient map in a center-of-momentum frame $\\Lambda P=(\\sqrt{s},\\mathbf0)$ as defined in [[lem-qft-example-two-body-phase-space]]. For one scalar initial label of weight $1$ and one specified final channel, take the dimensionless real quartic tree amplitude $\\mathcal A=-\\lambda$. The coefficient map of [[lem-qft-example-two-body-phase-space]] gives\n$$\\frac{d\\sigma_{\\mathrm{coeff}}}{d\\Omega} =\\frac{\\lambda^2(\\hbar c)^2}{128\\pi^2s}, \\qquad \\sigma_{\\mathrm{coeff}}=\\frac{\\lambda^2(\\hbar c)^2}{32\\pi s}$$\nfor identical final scalars integrated over the full labeled sphere. For distinguishable final scalars the two coefficients are twice these values.\n\nFor a parent at rest, $P_0=(\\mathsf M_0,\\mathbf0)$ with energy $\\mathsf M_0>2m$, decaying through a specified single channel to two identical scalars on the positive $m$-shell whose total four-vector is $P_0$, under a constant amplitude $G_E$ in joules, the rate coefficient is\n$$\\Gamma_{\\mathrm{coeff}} =\\frac{|G_E|^2}{32\\pi\\hbar\\mathsf M_0} \\sqrt{1-\\frac{4m^2}{\\mathsf M_0^2}}.$$\nThis result concerns the defined formal coefficients. It does not assert an exact exponential survival law.",
        "deps": [
          "def-qft-example-two-body-phase-space-data",
          "lem-qft-example-two-body-phase-space"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-qft-example-two-body-phase-space-data": "mathematical-premise",
