      {
        "id": "lem-qft-example-dirac-pauli-square",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "library": "mathematics",
        "title": "Minimal Dirac magnetic square and formal Pauli benchmark",
        "statement": "Let $m>0$ be a particle mass in kilograms, $q\\in\\mathbb R$ its charge in coulombs, and $A:\\mathbb R^3\\to\\mathbb R^3$ a smooth spatial vector potential with components in tesla-metres. Set $B_k=\\epsilon_{kij}\\partial_iA_j$ and define on the common core $\\mathcal C=C_c^\\infty(\\mathbb R^3;\\mathbb C^4)$\n$$\\pi_i=-i\\hbar\\partial_i-qA_i,\\qquad H_D=c\\sum_i\\alpha_i\\pi_i+\\beta mc^2,\\qquad \\Sigma_i=\\operatorname{diag}(\\sigma_i,\\sigma_i).$$\nHere the matrices are those of [[lem-qft-example-spin-trace-completeness]] and $\\hbar,c$ have the SI conventions of [[def-qft-example-data]]. These differential maps preserve $\\mathcal C$, and on $\\mathcal C$,\n$$[\\pi_i,\\pi_j]=iq\\hbar\\epsilon_{ijk}B_k,\\qquad H_D^2=m^2c^4I_4+c^2(\\boldsymbol\\pi^2-q\\hbar\\boldsymbol\\Sigma\\cdot\\mathbf B).$$\nIf the formal first-order square-root coefficient is written as $mc^2+K/(2m)$ with $K=\\boldsymbol\\pi^2-q\\hbar\\boldsymbol\\Sigma\\cdot\\mathbf B$, then its spin term is $-(q/m)\\mathbf S\\cdot\\mathbf B$, where $\\mathbf S=\\hbar\\boldsymbol\\Sigma/2$. Under the coefficient convention $H_{\\mathrm{mag}}=-\\boldsymbol\\mu_{\\mathrm{mag}}\\cdot\\mathbf B$ and $\\boldsymbol\\mu_{\\mathrm{mag}}=g_s(q/(2m))\\mathbf S$, equality of the formal coefficients as a linear function of $q$ gives $g_s=2$ for the minimal tree-level term. No magnetic self-adjoint closure, full spectrum, operator square-root theorem, radiative correction, or empirical prediction is asserted.",
        "deps": [
          "def-qft-example-data",
          "lem-qft-example-spin-trace-completeness"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-qft-example-data": "mathematical-premise",
          "lem-qft-example-spin-trace-completeness": "mathematical-premise"
        },
        "dependency_level": 3,
        "proof_strategy": "direct",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "literature-derived",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "Mark Srednicki, Quantum Field Theory, author-posted prepublication draft, section 64",
              "url": "https://web.physics.ucsb.edu/~mark/ms-qft-DRAFT.pdf",
              "locator": "Complete 616-page author-hosted textbook draft; printed pp. 383–385, minimally coupled Dirac electron and tree plus radiative magnetic-moment coefficients."
            },
            {
              "title": "David Tong, Quantum Field Theory, Chapter 4, sections 4.3 and 4.7",
              "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/qft/qfthtml/S4.html",
              "locator": "Complete author-hosted HTML chapter; Clifford matrices, Dirac equation, Pauli spinors, and positive-/negative-frequency solutions."
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
