        "library": "mathematics",
        "title": "Formal Dirac spin coefficient in a uniform field",
        "statement": "The two spin eigenvalues give opposite formal energy coefficients in the same uniform field. For comparison only, define the formal frequency coefficient $\\nu_{\\rm comp}:=eB_0/(2\\pi m)$, whose SI unit is $\\mathrm C\\,\\mathrm T\\,\\mathrm{kg}^{-1}=\\mathrm{s}^{-1}$, equivalently the formal angular-frequency coefficient $\\omega_{\\rm comp}:=2\\pi\\nu_{\\rm comp}=eB_0/m$. This is a formal comparison only, not a trajectory law or empirical prediction.",
